From 5d7830bc467e7109472bfe3ce1b237b5bfc3a3c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitor Machado <2932830+vittau@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:01:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Save the BOTH effects chip in quickstates and rewinds

Writer-routed BOTH mode instantiates a second YM2612 and a second SN76489
(chip 1) for the 68K SFX engine and the race SFX Z80 image. The quickstate
format carried only chip 0, so a state loaded into a process that was not
already running that race restored the 68K/Z80 machine into a pair of idle
effects chips: sustained FM voices (the engine sound started once by race
init) and the DAC stream stayed silent, while one-shot effects that key
themselves still played. Rewind snapshots had the same gap.

Chip 1 is written as an optional tagged, length-prefixed trailer after chip
0's unchanged bytes in ym2612_save_state/psg_save_state, and the loaders skip
it when it is absent, so a quickstate written by an older build still loads
and simply leaves chip 1 as it was (the old behaviour). Sections 4/5 of the
host state container may therefore be shorter than this build writes; the
loader validates them by reading, not by size. The rollback snapshots carry
both chips in the same shape.
